§§ `סעיף 348: הדין וחשבון השנתי`

-- The annual report is filed "once a year" (src:2974): the cadence is the text's own; the form and content are the Minister's ("כפי שיקבע השר").
-- The text names no day from which the year runs, so the layer starts the first year on the day the company registers under 346 (a fork, assumed, not ruled), and each later year on the day of the report before it.
-- A report not filed within its year is a BREACH BY the company: the text lays "תגיש" on the company by name. The first year is counted with the library's `add years` from the registration day, as the Boolean rule counts it from the previous report.
-- The later years are counted as 365 days from the previous report, because the previous report's date is not known when the clock is set (fork). Three yearly reports are encoded; after the third the rule stays open on a permission to file the next one.
-- Not a breach: a company that has stopped keeping the place of business and told the Registrar (349א(א)) owes no report, and the DEONTIC ends FULFILLED for it.
-- src:2974 | {{ח:ת}} חברת חוץ תגיש, אחת לשנה, דין וחשבון שנתי כפי שיקבע השר.
-- FORK: סעיף 348 | the year runs from the day the company registers under 346 (the text names no start day: assumed, not ruled), then from each report to the next | no clock on the first report, as the Boolean rule `סעיף 348 - חברת חוץ הגישה דין וחשבון שנתי כנדרש` answers NOTHING until a previous report exists
-- FORK: סעיף 348 | a report missed within its year is a terminal BREACH BY the company ("תגיש" lays the duty on the company by name, and "אחת לשנה" fixes the cadence) | the Minister's power ("כפי שיקבע השר") leaves the timing to the Minister, so a late report is no breach
-- FORK: סעיף 348 | the first year is `add years` from the registration day; each later year is 365 days from the previous report, since that report's date is not known when the clock is set (the Boolean rule counts `add years` from the previous report, which differs by a day where the year spans a 29 February) | every year by `add years`
-- FORK: סעיף 348 | three yearly reports are encoded; after the third the rule stays open on a permission to file the next report, which stands for the later years not encoded here | an unbounded chain of yearly duties
-- FORK: סעיף 348 | the duty binds every foreign company until it has stopped keeping a place of business in Israel and told the Registrar (349א(א) is the text's own exit) | the duty binds only a company registered under 346 and not yet exempt
-- FORK: סעיף 348 | a report not in the form the Minister set does not count, so the duty stays open and its year runs on to a BREACH (the guard is the Boolean `הדין וחשבון הוגש בנוסח שקבע השר`) | such a report discharges the duty
-- TIMELINE: unit=calendar day; day 0=the day the company registers under 346 (assumed, not ruled); counting="אחת לשנה" (the first year by `add years` from the registration day, each later year 365 days from the previous report)
@ref סעיף 348 דין וחשבון שנתי (src:2974-2974)
GIVEN `מועד הרישום כחברת חוץ` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`סעיף 348 - מספר הימים עד הדין וחשבון הראשון` MEANS
    (Day (`add years` `מועד הרישום כחברת חוץ` 1)) MINUS (Day `מועד הרישום כחברת חוץ`)

-- One yearly report, numbered from 1: the company MUST file it within the days given; filing it opens the next year's report.
-- A report that is not filed in time is a BREACH BY the company; after the third report the rule stays open on a permission to file the next (the later years are not encoded here).
@ref סעיף 348 דין וחשבון שנתי (src:2974-2974)
